# Build setting read by no rule, set only by the `pruned_inputs.bzl` analysis
# tests (see that file): it puts the target under test in a configuration no
# build uses, so `unused_inputs_list` pruning from an executed build can never
# rewrite the inputs those tests inspect. The default (`False`) keeps every
# normal, `-c dbg`, and hermeticity build on the shared configuration.
